course: dictionary
lesson: 5096
title: Breaking words apart
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are built from smaller parts, and each part has a meaning. «Interfaith friendship means people of different beliefs learning about each other and serving the community together.» The sentence tells you the friendship is between people of different beliefs, so interfaith must mean between faiths.
explain: Split the word into parts. Inter means between, as in «international». Faith means belief, or a religion. Put the parts together and you get between faiths. This trick works on many words, so look for the small parts first.
explain: Then check your meaning in the sentence. Swap in between faiths: «Interfaith friendship means people of different beliefs learning about each other.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Interfaith means between or among people of different religions.
fact: The religions can include Christians, Jews, Muslims, Hindus, Sikhs and Buddhists.
fact: An interfaith event brings different faiths together to meet, talk, pray or work for good causes.
fact: «Interfaith dialogue» means people of different faiths talking together to understand each other.
fact: Inter means between, and faith means belief, so the parts of the word help you guess its meaning.
exercise: «Interfaith friendship means people of different beliefs learning about each other.» What does interfaith mean? | Only with people who share one belief | *Between people of different religions | Inside a church | Between people who all live on the same street
exercise: Which of these is an interfaith event? | A school quiz about maths | *Hindus, Jews and Buddhists meeting together to talk and work on a food bank | A single family praying quietly at home | A school trip to the seaside
exercise: Find and copy the word that means between faiths in «an interfaith service». | service | *interfaith | an | the
test: Which of these is one of the faiths named in the meaning of interfaith? | Scientists | Vikings | *Buddhists | Farmers
test: What is the best meaning of «interfaith week»? | A week off school for holidays | *A week when people of different beliefs come together to learn and help | A week of only sports | A week when everyone must go to the same church
exam: Why might a school arrange an interfaith visit? | So pupils can skip their lessons | So everyone must choose one religion | *So pupils can learn about and respect different places of worship | So the school can buy new desks
